Forager: forest wins over bare rock in the landuse layer (dispatch 2026-10-22-pi-30, with its amendment 1)

Against protomaps/basemaps at ca93fc06efbaff1c5f069d06edbe5de18839c1c8 (tiles 4.15.2), with
0001-roads-trail-attributes.patch already applied. Applied after 0001 with `git apply` from the
repository root by map-build/bin/build-basemap-jar.sh.

Why this departs from upstream: OSM data sometimes tags a forest with natural=bare_rock too
(r14965119 near Seaside, OR, 2026-10-22); Forager prefers the landuse forest/wood kind. Owner's
ruling, relayed by Rowan and confirmed in the cartography planner session. landuse=wood is not an
upstream landuse kind, so wood + bare_rock is left as bare_rock.

Upstream takes kind from the last matching rule (Matcher.getString walks the matches reversed), so
the natural rule, after the landuse rule, made such an area bare_rock. bare_rock leaves the natural
rule's list and gets a rule of its own right after it that does not match landuse=forest. Nothing
else changes. The parameterized test foragerForestOverBareRock (4 cases) in LanduseTest pins it.

